 incomes average  a mere 675 thousand bucks apiece  low-income families those people between  1978 and 1992 they as a result of the  tax cuts that they received added one  trillion dollars to the national debt  one trillion dollars in tax cuts the  same fuddy study found that the same 1  million families the richest people in  America pay 30% less of their incomes in  taxes than they would have had the 1977  tax code remained in existence so what  does that tell us  when we look for funding for feeding  hungry children for putting people into  affordable housing it means to me that  the time is now in a very strong way to  say the wealthiest people in this  country they're going to have to start  paying their fair share of taxes  and that means to my mind going much  higher than raising the income tax rate  from 31 to 36 percent it means among  other things we should go higher than  that it means that we must create a  progressive corporate tax rate it means  we must be prepared to do way with much  of the tax deductibility for business  meals and entertainment some of our  friends were able to write off going to  the country clubs are going to finally  start having to look at the hungry  children on the sidewalk as they go to  the country club and maybe maybe pay a  tax on that and it means doing away with  the tax breaks that now exists to help  companies acquire runaway plants that  move out of the country and also I think  that the time is right that we even may  have to contemplate going be beyond just  an income tax and talk about a tax on  wealth I think that that's appropriate  as well  secondly when we talk about how we're  going to raise the money that we need it  is absolutely imperative and impossible  not to look at the bloated military  budget I think very few people have  illusions that the world we're living in  now is wonderful is perfectly safe that  we should disarm America nobody thinks  that but on the other hand there is some  excellent news the fact of the matter is  that the Cold War is over a longtime  adversary the Soviet Union does not  exist Russia wants to join NATO Russia  has significantly cut down on their  military spending lack while lesser is  no longer in jail in Poland he's the  president of the country  East Germany is no longer threatening  West Germany it is part of West Germany  and so forth and so on in my view and  the view of people who know more about  this than I do this country today can  very safely reduce military spending by  50 percent over the next four years  and use those hundreds of billions of  dollars in freedom money to reinvest in  America and to deal with the deficit  let me also touch very briefly when we  talk about how we are going to acquire  some money it's always a funny thing you  know when we need money for hungry  children when we need money to create  productive jobs they always tell us  there's not money available but you know  what when they wanted a war in the  Persian Gulf no problem  plenty of money available and let me  tell you someplace else where there's  always money available in the next  couple of months unless I'm very  mistaken president Democrats Republicans  are going to come before the people and  say they need another 40 or 50 billion  dollars to bail out the Savings and Loan  industry  well the 40 or 50 billion dollars now I  happen to think that with all of this  talk about the deficit and how we may  have to ask senior citizens to take cuts  and colas and raise middle income taxes  and gas taxes and so forth and so  everybody is so concerned about the  deficit why the hell are we dumping  another forty billion dollars into the  deficit to bail out the savings and loan  industry makes sense to anybody here all  right so I think that there are fairer  and more progressive ways to deal with  the S&amp;L bailout than to dump it into the  deficit let me simply conclude and pick  up a point I think that Nydia less was  made earlier and that is that we now  have the potential to make some very  fundamental changes in this country but  we cannot do it unless we come together  and stand up and fight 45% of the people  don't vote poor people don't vote many  working people don't vote our voices are  not being heard the good news is that  after twelve years reaganomics is gone  but don't anybody think that there is  not an enormous struggle in front of us  so my hope is that those of us in  Congress those of in the unions of the  Women's Committee all of you that we all  begin to stand together and say that  this country has the potential the  the best country that they ever was and  we can do that if we stand together and  let's do that  thank you very much
 

